Note that mathlib is the standard Eathon mathematics module providing reusable functions and recursion.

To compute absVal taking x as integer returning integer,
  If x is less than 0 then,
    Return neg x.
  End if.
  Return x.
End function.

To compute maxVal taking a as integer, b as integer returning integer,
  If a is greater than b then,
    Return a.
  End if.
  Return b.
End function.

To compute minVal taking a as integer, b as integer returning integer,
  If a is less than b then,
    Return a.
  End if.
  Return b.
End function.

To compute clampVal taking val as integer, low as integer, high as integer returning integer,
  If val is less than low then,
    Return low.
  End if.
  If val is greater than high then,
    Return high.
  End if.
  Return val.
End function.

To compute power taking base as integer, exp as integer returning integer,
  If exp is at most 0 then,
    Return 1.
  End if.
  Let prevExp be exp minus 1.
  Call power with base, prevExp into subPower.
  Return base times subPower.
End function.

To compute factorial taking n as integer returning integer,
  If n is at most 1 then,
    Return 1.
  End if.
  Let prevN be n minus 1.
  Call factorial with prevN into subFact.
  Return n times subFact.
End function.
